            "created_at": "2025-09-09T00:36:15.929196+00:00",
            "notes": "[Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b) should be your second purple, it offers a ton of value and charges up from your biotic grasp (weapon damage) or biotic energy healing \u2013 not your orb. Because of how often your weapon damage/healing ticks though, it's easy to have it at max stacks the majority of the time.\n\nIf you feel like you *really* need the extra boost in biotic energy, you can pick up [Alternative Energy](item_c3e816b3-9c39-4528-9578-e3fa610b6cc6), but I find it to be a lower value pick that encourages bad habits. If you're using your damage orbs on cooldown, shooting the orbs from [Optimal Overflow](item_9d85ca48-b27a-435a-8ef9-247440e0f97d) even in the general direction of the enemy, and using your biotic grasp as a filler, you shouldn't find yourself running out of biotic energy when you need it very often. [High Capacity Tubing](item_d4779a06-a19c-425d-80ff-159fde15a3f2) or [Bio-Needles](item_fc8b5d34-98ab-412f-9e01-768d1986507f) are cheaper stop-gap solutions if you feel like you need just a little bit of extra help from keeping your biotic energy reserves from running dry.\n\nYou can also opt for [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) to pressure the enemy even more by applying healing reduction across their whole team more effectively than probably any other hero in Stadium. If you've been pumping, you can potentially afford it now in addition to [Superflexor](item_580b77b4-0d63-469b-99a8-5372c55dfc1b), but it's not essential to buy it now.\n\nBecause you're sending out orbs so often, this should be up pretty often on the enemy team as-is. Because of that, I go with [Precarious Potency](item_b1305ee6-3027-4131-8797-dcbeb68e3953) as the third power in most games, to help keep your team's health topped-up more easily. But if you feel like you need the healing suppression to be up more consistently, or you're still getting the hang of aiming your orbs to keep them on the enemy most of the time, getting [Multiball](item_5d0e4135-f4e1-42fb-991a-417643064560) now is an option.",
